      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "To a mixed CH3CN/CH3OH (10 mL, v/v = 1:1) solution containing mpkoH (82.3 mg, 0.6 mmol) and triethylamine (60.7 mg, 0.6 mmol) was slowly added Ni(ClO4)2·6H2O (73.1 mg, 0.2 mmol) and Dy(NO3)3·6H2O (45.7 mg, 0.1 mmol). The resulting red mixture was transferred into a Teflon-lined stainless steel vessel (23.0 mL) and heated at 80 °C for 24 h. After cooling to room temperature at 1.7 K·h−1, red block-shaped crystals suitable for X-ray analysis were obtained directly, washed with cold methanol, and dried in air.",
