      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Antiferromagnetically coupled hexanuclear {Dy3Ni3} cluster. χMT at 300 K is 46.13 cm3·K·mol−1 (1.0 kOe), close to the isolated-ion expectation, and falls to 32.85 cm3·K·mol−1 at 2.0 K. Magnetization at 2.0 K and 70 kOe is 24.48 Nβ, well below the 36.00 Nβ saturation value, consistent with DyIII anisotropy. Zero-dc-field ac susceptibility (3.5 Oe oscillating field) shows frequency-dependent χ′ and χ″ below 10 K, indicating slow magnetization relaxation, but no clear χ″ maxima even under 3 kOe dc field because of QTM. Debye estimation gives ΔE/kB ≈ 4.1 K and τ0 ≈ 6.9×10−8 s.",
        "measurements": [
